<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Experimental Configuration and Methodology Details</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Language Model Configuration</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We employ GPT-3.5-Turbo, GPT-4o-mini, Gemini-1.5-flash, and GPT-4o as our evaluation models with a sampling temperature of 0.7.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Dataset Preprocessing</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All experimental datasets are utilized in their original, unmodified public formats.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Node Generation Configuration</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our experimental framework, we systematically controll the node generation process by setting a critical hyperparameter <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. The number of node generation is constrained to <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3</annotation></semantics></math>, a carefully chosen value that strikes an optimal balance between comprehensive reasoning and computational efficiency.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Node Selection Strategy</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our node exploration methodology utilizes a structured three-tier categorization system, as illustrated in Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ A.4 Node Selection Strategy ‣ Appendix A Experimental Configuration and Methodology Details ‣ Mission Impossible: Feedback-Guided Dynamic Interactive Planning for Improving Reasoning on LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. This hierarchical selection approach optimizes computational resources by focusing on the most promising reasoning pathways.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T4" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A1.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Category</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T4.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:138.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Description</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T4.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:103.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.2.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Exploration Strategy</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T4.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">“Sure”</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:138.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Nodes with high probability of leading to correct answers</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:103.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Prioritized for immediate expansion</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">“Maybe”</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:138.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Nodes with uncertain but potential relevance</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:103.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Conditionally explored based on context</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">“Impossible”</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:138.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Nodes demonstrably unlikely to contribute to solution</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:103.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Immediately pruned from exploration path</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Node selection categorization strategy.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Model Generalizability Experiments</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the generalizability of FGDIP, we conduct additional experiments on a range of language models beyond GPT-3.5-Turbo. The results demonstrate FGDIP’s effectiveness across different model sizes and architectures.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate FGDIP on the HotpotQA dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2018</a>)</cite> using three additional language models: GPT-4o-mini, Gemini-1.5-flash, and GPT-4o. The experimental setup and evaluation metrics are consistent with those described in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Experimental Configuration and Methodology Details ‣ Mission Impossible: Feedback-Guided Dynamic Interactive Planning for Improving Reasoning on LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Results</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ B.2 Results ‣ Appendix B Model Generalizability Experiments ‣ Mission Impossible: Feedback-Guided Dynamic Interactive Planning for Improving Reasoning on LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> presents the F1 scores achieved by different methods on the HotpotQA dataset across the evaluated models.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T5" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A2.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A2.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></th>
<th id="A2.T5.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T5.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPT-4o-mini</span></th>
<th id="A2.T5.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T5.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gemini-1.5-flash</span></th>
<th id="A2.T5.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T5.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPT-4o</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T5.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Standard</th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">21.69</td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">22.36</td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">45.50</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">CoT</th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">38.72</td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">32.30</td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">58.82</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">UALA</th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">42.10</td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">-</td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">59.95</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_b">FGDIP (Ours)</th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b"><span id="A2.T5.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">45.37</span></td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b"><span id="A2.T5.2.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">45.62</span></td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b"><span id="A2.T5.2.5.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">65.69</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Comparison of F1 score performance of different methods on the HotpotQA dataset (%). UALA’s reliance on the logprobs parameter restricts its use to specific models like the GPT series. Our framework is applicable to other models like Claude and Gemini.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The results demonstrate that FGDIP consistently outperforms baseline methods across all tested models. On smaller models like GPT-4o-mini and Gemini-1.5-flash, FGDIP achieves F1 scores of 45.37% and 45.62%, respectively, showcasing its effectiveness even with limited computational resources. In addition, the performance improvement on Gemini-1.5-flash is particularly obvious, which shows the potential of FGDIP on small and medium models.
On the larger GPT-4o model, FGDIP achieves an F1 score of 65.69%, a significant improvement over its performance on GPT-3.5-Turbo, indicating that FGDIP scales effectively with model size. Larger models are better able to leverage the dynamic and adaptive reasoning capabilities of FGDIP.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, unlike the UALA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Han et al., 2024</a>)</cite> method, which is limited to models providing access to log probabilities (e.g., the GPT series), FGDIP demonstrates broad applicability across different model architectures. While Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ B.2 Results ‣ Appendix B Model Generalizability Experiments ‣ Mission Impossible: Feedback-Guided Dynamic Interactive Planning for Improving Reasoning on LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> focuses on GPT series models for direct comparison with UALA, FGDIP’s design allows it to be used with other models, such as Claude and Gemini.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
