<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Prompt</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Prompt to Extract Key Entities </h3>

<figure id="A5.T11" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A5.T11.2" class="ltx_tabular">
<tr id="A5.T11.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"><span id="A5.T11.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Extract one or more key entities based on a multi-hop problem so that the agent can try to solve the problem starting from a certain key entity.
Your task is to identify and extract well-defined entities in a complex information environment. When faced with a problem that contains multiple entities, you need to distinguish which entities are specific and unique, and which entities may refer to broad concepts or categories. Directive entities are usually individually identifiable names of people, places, specific events or unique objects, and they have clear definitions and boundaries in the context. In contrast, generic entities are more vague, such as common nouns or broad categories that can cover many specific instances. Your task is to focus on those clear entities, identify their role and importance in a given problem, and distinguish them from broader or vague concepts.</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T11.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T11.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T11.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T11.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Here are some examples:</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T11.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T11.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T11.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T11.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Question: Geoff LaTulippe is an American writer whose best-known work was directed by whom?</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T11.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T11.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T11.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T11.p4.1" class="ltx_p">["Geoff LaTulippe"]</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T11.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T11.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T11.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T11.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Question: What is the population of the city which Deryl Dedmon came from?</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T11.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T11.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T11.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T11.p6.1" class="ltx_p">["Deryl Dedmon"]</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T11.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T11.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T11.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T11.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Question: Who is older Danny Green or James Worthy?</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T11.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T11.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T11.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T11.p8.1" class="ltx_p">["Danny Green","James Worthy"]</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T11.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T11.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T11.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T11.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Question: Alfie Allen played Theon Greyjoy on which show?</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T11.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T11.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T11.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T11.p10.1" class="ltx_p">["Alfie Allen","Theon Greyjoy"]</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T11.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T11.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T11.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T11.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Question: The Bragg–Gray cavity theory was developed by Louis Harold Gray, William Lawrence Bragg, and a man that was knighted in what year?</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T11.2.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.2.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T11.2.12.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T11.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T11.p12.1" class="ltx_p">["Bragg–Gray cavity theory", "Louis Harold Gray", "William Lawrence Bragg"]</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T11.2.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.2.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T11.2.13.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T11.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T11.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Question: Which battle took place during the American Civil War, Battle of Gettysburg or Battle of Tarawa?</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T11.2.14" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.2.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b"><span id="A5.T11.2.14.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T11.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T11.p14.1" class="ltx_p">["American Civil War", "Battle of Gettysburg", "Battle of Tarawa"]</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.T12" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 12: </span>Prompt used for extracting key entities.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Prompt to Evaluate Step</h3>

<figure id="A5.T13" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A5.T13.2" class="ltx_tabular">
<tr id="A5.T13.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T13.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"><span id="A5.T13.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T13.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a series of steps involving thought, action, and observation that have been undertaken. Assess the likelihood that continuing such steps over time would lead to the correct answer (sure/maybe/impossible), instead of evaluating the likelihood of getting the answer right away in the next step.</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T13.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T13.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T13.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T13.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
