<span id="A5.T13.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T13.p20.1" class="ltx_p">Action 2: Lookup[developed]</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T13.2.22" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T13.2.22.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T13.2.22.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T13.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T13.p21.1" class="ltx_p">Observation 2: (Result 1 / 1) The initial game was developed by Daniel Kahneman in the 1980s and involved three parties, with one active and two passive participants.</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T13.2.23" class="ltx_tr">
