<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Prompt to Evaluate Answer</h3>

<figure id="A5.T15" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A5.T15.2" class="ltx_tabular">
<tr id="A5.T15.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"><span id="A5.T15.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p1.1" class="ltx_p">You will be given QUESTION and Get_answer. You need to check whether the type of Get_answer provided is consistent with the question. You need to identify the possible answer to the QUESTION, and then check whether the Get_answer is the possible ANSWER.</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For every case, you must think firstly in THOUGHT, and then output your JUDGMENT, with the format:</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p3.1" class="ltx_p">THOUGHT: (your analysis here).</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p4.1" class="ltx_p">JUDGMENT: YES / NO</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Please note that the answer must directly answer the question. If the answer is ’unknown’ or other words that indicate uncertainty and do not actually answer the question, then your judgment should be ’NO’.</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Here are some examples:</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Question: What is the elevation range for the area that the eastern sector of the Colorado orogeny extends into?</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Get_answer: 1,800 to 7,000 ft</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p9.1" class="ltx_p">THOUGHT: The eastern sector of the Colorado orogeny would have a specific elevation range, usually expressed in feet or meters. The given ANSWER "1,800 to 7,000 ft" specifies a range in feet, which is a plausible elevation range for an orogenic area. Therefore, this seems like a possible answer to the QUESTION about the elevation range of the area affected by the Colorado orogeny.</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p10.1" class="ltx_p">JUDGMENT: YES</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.12.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Question: Which continent have a distribution of both the Ternstroemia and Cussonia genus of plants?</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.13.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Get_answer: Africa</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.14" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.14.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p13.1" class="ltx_p">THOUGHT: The Ternstroemia and Cussonia genera of plants would be distributed in specific geographical regions, which could include one or more continents. The ANSWER "Africa" is given as the continent where both these genera are found. If both the Ternstroemia and Cussonia genera have a known distribution in Africa, then this answer would be correct.</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.15" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.15.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p14.1" class="ltx_p">JUDGMENT: YES</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.16" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.16.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.17" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.17.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.17.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p15.1" class="ltx_p">Question: Where is the head quarter of the Blue Bird Body Company?</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.18" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.18.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.18.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p16.1" class="ltx_p">Get_answer: Fort Valley, Georgia</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.19" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.19.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.19.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p17.1" class="ltx_p">THOUGHT: The Blue Bird Body Company is known for manufacturing school buses and other vehicles, and its headquarters location is a specific factual piece of information. The given ANSWER is "Fort Valley, Georgia," which, based on my existing knowledge, is correct. The Blue Bird Body Company is indeed headquartered in Fort Valley, Georgia.</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.20" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.20.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.20.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p18.1" class="ltx_p">JUDGMENT: YES</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.21" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.21.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.22" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.22.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.22.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p19.1" class="ltx_p">Question: In what country did Gildo Siopaes win a bronze medal for bobsledding in the 1964 Winter Olympics?</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.23" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.23.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.23.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p20.1" class="ltx_p">Get_answer: Italy</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.24" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.24.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.24.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p21.1" class="ltx_p">THOUGHT: The question asks about the country where Gildo Siopaes won a bronze medal in bobsledding during the 1964 Winter Olympics. The ANSWER provided is "Italy." However, there is issue here. Athletes win medals for their country, not in a country, unless it’s asking about the location of the event. The 1964 Winter Olympics were held in Innsbruck, Austria, not Italy. It seems the question might be mixing details about an athlete’s nationality with the location of the event or has incorrect details.</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.25" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.25.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.25.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p22.1" class="ltx_p">JUDGMENT: NO</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.26" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.26.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.27" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.27.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.27.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p23.1" class="ltx_p">Question: The 1978 NBA World Championship Series had as MVP which Hall of Fame class member of 1988?</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.28" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.28.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.28.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p24.1" class="ltx_p">Get_answer: yes</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.29" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.29.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.29.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p25" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p25.1" class="ltx_p">THOUGHT: The question is asking for the name of the person who was awarded MVP of the 1978 NBA World Championship Series and who was later inducted into the Hall of Fame in 1988. The correct answer should be the name of an individual, specifically a basketball player. The given ANSWER "yes" does not fulfill the requirement of naming the individual; it’s merely an affirmation and does not provide the necessary information.</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.30" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.30.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.30.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p26" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p26.1" class="ltx_p">JUDGMENT: NO</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.31" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.31.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.32" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.32.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.32.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p27" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p27.1" class="ltx_p">Question: Which Nobel laureate in Literature, known for exploring themes of existentialism, wrote a novel set during a plague in Algeria?</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.33" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.33.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.33.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p28" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p28.1" class="ltx_p">Get_answer: Albert Einstein</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.34" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.34.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="A5.T15.2.34.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p29" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p29.1" class="ltx_p">THOUGHT: The question asks for a Nobel laureate in Literature who wrote about existential themes and set a novel during a plague in Algeria. The correct answer is Albert Camus, specifically for his novel "The Plague." Albert Einstein, on the other hand, was a physicist known for his contributions to the theory of relativity and quantum mechanics, and he was awarded the Nobel Prize in Physics, not Literature. Additionally, Einstein did not author novels. Thus, the ANSWER provided fails to correspond correctly to the question regarding a literary work and author.</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T15.2.35" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T15.2.35.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b"><span id="A5.T15.2.35.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:310.5pt;">
<span id="A5.T15.p30" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.T15.p30.1" class="ltx_p">JUDGMENT: NO</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
